        docs: '```coffeescript [specscript]\n' +
          'createContainer(options {\n' +
          '  name: string,\n' +
          '  image: string,\n' +
          '  rm: boolean,\n' +
          "  restart: 'no'|'on-failure[:<max-retries>]'|'always'|'unless-stopped',\n" +
          "  logDriver: 'local'|'json-file'|'syslog'|'journald'|'gelf'|'fluentd'|'awslogs'|'splunk'|'etwlogs'|'none',\n" +
          '  logDriverOptions: Object<string>,\n' +
          '  publish: Object<\n' +
          '    [hostPort string]: containerPort string # 8080\n' +
          `      |containerPortWithProtocol string # '<containerPort>[/<"tcp"|"udp"|"sctp">]'\n` +
          '  >,\n' +
          '  healthCmd: Array<string>,\n' +
          '  healthInterval: number, # nanoseconds, minimum 1e6, default 10e9\n' +
          '  healthTimeout: number, # nanoseconds, minimum 1e6, default 20e9\n' +
          '  healthRetries: number, # default 5\n' +
          '  healthStartPeriod: number, # nanoseconds, minimum 1e6\n' +
          '  memory: number, # bytes\n' +
          '  cpus: number,\n' +
          '  mounts: Array<{\n' +
          '    source: string,\n' +
          '    target: string,\n' +
          '    readonly: boolean,\n' +
          "    type: 'bind'|'cluster'|'image'|'npipe'|'tmpfs'|'volume',\n" +
          '  }>|Array<\n' +
          "    mount string, # '<source>:<target>[:<readonly true|false>]'\n" +
          '  >,\n' +
          '\n' +
          '  # Dockerfile defaults\n' +
          '  cmd: Array<string|number>,\n' +
          `  expose: Array<port string>, # '<port>[/<"tcp"|"udp"|"sctp">]'\n` +
          '  volume: Array<path string>,\n' +
          '  workdir: path string,\n' +
          '  env: Object<string>,\n' +
          '}) -> data Promise<{\n' +
          '  Id: string,\n' +
          '  Warnings: Array<string>,\n' +
          '}>\n' +
          '```\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Creates a Docker container.\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Arguments:\n' +
          '  * `options`\n' +
          '    * `name` - the name that will be assigned to the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `image` - the name and tag of the image.\n' +
          '    * `rm` - automatically remove the Docker container when it exits.\n' +
          '    * `restart` - the restart policy for the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `logDriver` - the logging driver used for the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `logDriverOptions` - driver-specific configuration options for the logging driver.\n' +
          '    * `publish` - object of mappings of host ports to container ports with optional protocols.\n' +
          '    * `healthCmd` - a command that checks the health of the Docker container. The health check fails if the command errors. The command is run inside the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `healthInterval` - time in nanoseconds to wait between healthchecks.\n' +
          '    * `healthTimeout` - time in nanoseconds to wait before the healthcheck fails.\n' +
          '    * `healthRetries` - number of times to retry the health check before the Docker container is considered unhealhty.\n' +
          '    * `healthStartPeriod` - time in nanoseconds to wait when the Docker container starts up before running the first health check command.\n' +
          '    * `memory` - memory limit of the Docker container in bytes.\n' +
          '    * `cpus` - CPU quota in CPUs.\n' +
          "    * `mounts` - specification of the Docker container's volumes or mounts\n" +
          '      * `source` - the mount source (e.g. a volume name or a host path).\n' +
          '      * `target` - the mounted path inside the Docker container.\n' +
          '      * `readonly`- if `true`, the mount is read-only. If `false`, the mount is writable. Defaults to `false`.\n' +
          '      * `type` - the mount type.\n' +
          '    * `cmd` - the command that is run by the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `expose` - an array of ports with optional protocols that the Docker container exposes.\n' +
          '    * `volume` - an array of mount point paths inside the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `workdir` - the working directory of the Docker container.\n' +
          "    * `env` - an object of the Docker container's environment variables. Maps environment variable names to environment variable values, e.g. `{ FOO: 'bar' }`.\n" +
          '\n' +
          'Return:\n' +
          '  * `data`\n' +
          '    * `Id` - the ID of the Docker container.\n' +
          '    * `Warnings` - warnings encountered when creating the Docker container.\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Restart policies:\n' +
          '  * `no` - do not restart the Docker container when it exits\n' +
          '  * `on-failure` - restart only if container exits with non-zero exit code\n' +
          '  * `always` - always restart container regardless of exit code\n' +
          '  * `unless-stopped` - like `always` except if the Docker container was put into a stopped state before the Docker daemon was stopped\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Health checks:\n' +
          '  * `[]` - inherit healthcheck from image or parent image\n' +
          "  * `['NONE']` - disable healthcheck\n" +
          "  * `['CMD', ...args]` - exec arguments directly\n" +
          "  * `['CMD-SHELL', command string]` - run command with system's default shell\n" +
          '\n' +
          'Mount types:\n' +
          '  * `bind` - mounts a file or directory from the host into the Docker container. The `source` must exist prior to creating the Docker container.\n' +
          '  * `cluster` - a Docker Swarm cluster volume.\n' +
          '  * `image` - mounts a Docker image.\n' +
          '  * `npipe` - mounts a named pipe from the host into the Docker container.\n' +
          '  * `tmpfs` - create a tmpfs with the given options. The `source` cannot be specified with mount type `tmpfs`.\n' +
          '  * `volume` - creates a volume with the given name and options or uses a pre-existing volume with the same name and options. The volume persists when the Docker container is removed.\n' +
          '\n' +
          '```javascript\n' +
          'const docker = new Docker()\n' +
          '\n' +
          'const data = await docker.createContainer({\n' +
          "  image: 'node:15-alpine',\n" +
          "  cmd: ['node', '-e', 'console.log(\\'Hello World.\\')'],\n" +
          '  rm: true,\n' +
          '})\n' +
          '```',
