    name: 'DynamoDBStream',
    docs: '```coffeescript [specscript]\n' +
      'new DynamoDBStream(options {\n' +
      '  table: string,\n' +
      '  accessKeyId: string,\n' +
      '  secretAccessKey: string,\n' +
      '  region: string,\n' +
      '  autoReady: boolean,\n' +
      "  StreamViewType: 'NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES'|'NEW_IMAGE'|'OLD_IMAGE'|'KEYS_ONLY',\n" +
      "  ShardIteratorType: 'TRIM_HORIZON'|'LATEST',\n" +
      '  GetRecordsLimit: number,\n' +
      '  GetRecordsInterval: number,\n' +
      '  ShardUpdatePeriod: number,\n' +
      '  ListStreamsLimit: number,\n' +
      '  JSON: boolean,\n' +
      '}) -> stream DynamoDBStream\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      "Presidium DynamoDBStream client for [AWS DynamoDB](https://aws.amazon.com/dynamodb/). Creates the DynamoDB Stream if it doesn't exist.\n" +
      '\n' +
      'DynamoDBStream instances have a `ready` promise that resolves when the DynamoDB Stream is active.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Arguments:\n' +
      '  * `options`\n' +
      '    * `table` - the name of the DynamoDB Table to which the DynamoDB Stream belongs.\n' +
      '    * `accessKeyId` - the AWS access key id.\n' +
      '    * `secretAccessKey` - the AWS secret access key.\n' +
      '    * `region` - the AWS region.\n' +
      "    * `autoReady` - whether to automatically create the DynamoDB Stream if it doesn't exist. Defaults to `true`.\n" +
      '    * `StreamViewType` - determines what information is written to the DynamoDB Stream.\n' +
      "    * `ShardIteratorType` - determines how the shard iterator is used to start reading stream records from a shard of the stream. A shard is a replica of a stream for enhanced throughput purposes. Defaults to `'LATEST'`.\n" +
      '    * `GetRecordsLimit` - number of records to fetch per DynamoDB Streams GetRecords operation. Defaults to `1000`.\n' +
      '    * `GetRecordsInterval` - number of milliseconds to wait between DynamoDB Streams GetRecords calls. Defaults to `1000`.\n' +
      '    * `ShardUpdatePeriod` - number of milliseconds to wait between shard updates. Defaults to `15000`.\n' +
      '    * `ListStreamsLimit` - number of streams to list per DynamoDB Streams ListStreams calls. Defaults to `100`.\n' +
      '    * `JSON` - replaces `NewImage` in DynamoDB JSON format with `NewImageJSON` in JSON format and `OldImage` in DynamoDB JSON format with `OldImageJSON` in JSON format for all stream records. Defaults to `false`.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`StreamViewType` values:\n' +
      '  * `KEYS_ONLY` - only the key attributes of the modified item are written to the DynamoDB Stream.\n' +
      '  * `NEW_IMAGE` - the entire item after it was modified is written to the DynamoDB Stream.\n' +
      '  * `OLD_IMAGE` - the entire item before it was modified is written to the DynamoDB Stream.\n' +
      '  * `NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES` - both the entire item before it was modified and the entire item after it was modified is written to the DynamoDB Stream.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`ShardIteratorType` values:\n' +
      '  * `TRIM_HORIZON` - start reading at the last (untrimmed) stream record, which is the oldest record in the stream shard. In DynamoDB Streams, there is a 24 hour limit on data retention. Stream records older than this limit are subject to removal (trimming) from the DynamoDB Stream.\n' +
      '  * `LATEST` - start reading just after the most recent stream record in the stream shard, so that the most recent data in the shard is always read.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Return:\n' +
      '  * `stream` - a DynamoDBStream instance.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```javascript\n' +
      "const awsCreds = await AwsCredentials('my-profile')\n" +
      "awsCreds.region = 'us-east-1'\n" +
      '\n' +
      'const env = process.env.NODE_ENV\n' +
      '\n' +
      'const myTable = new DynamoTable({\n' +
      '  name: `${env}-my-table`,\n' +
      "  key: [{ id: 'string' }],\n" +
      '  ...awsCreds,\n' +
      '})\n' +
      'await myTable.ready\n' +
      '\n' +
      'const myStream = new DynamoDBStream({\n' +
      '  table: `${env}-my-table`,\n' +
      '  ...awsCreds,\n' +
      '})\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'References:\n' +
      '  * [DynamoDB Streams](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/Streams.html)',
