        name: 'listObjects',
        docs: '```coffeescript [specscript]\n' +
          'listObjects(options {\n' +
          '  Delimiter: string,\n' +
          "  EncodingType: 'url',\n" +
          '  MaxKeys: number,\n' +
          '  Prefix: string,\n' +
          '  ContinuationToken: string,\n' +
          '  FetchOwner: boolean,\n' +
          '  StartAfter: string,\n' +
          '}) -> data Promise<{\n' +
          '  IsTruncated: boolean,\n' +
          '  Contents: Array<{\n' +
          '    Key: string,\n' +
          '    LastModified: Date,\n' +
          '    ETag: string,\n' +
          "    ChecksumAlgorithm: 'CRC32'|'CRC32C'|'SHA1'|'SHA256',\n" +
          '    Size: number, # bytes\n' +
          "    StorageClass: 'STANDARD'|'REDUCED_REDUNDANCY'|'STANDARD_IA'|'ONEZONE_IA'\n" +
          "                  |'INTELLIGENT_TIERING'|'GLACIER'|'DEEP_ARCHIVE'|'OUTPOSTS'\n" +
          "                  |'GLACIER_IR'|'SNOW'|'EXPRESS_ONEZONE',\n" +
          '    Owner: {\n' +
          '      DisplayName: string,\n' +
          '      ID: string\n' +
          '    },\n' +
          '  }>,\n' +
          '  CommonPrefixes: Array<{ Prefix: string }>,\n' +
          '  KeyCount: number,\n' +
          '  NextContinuationToken: string,\n' +
          '}>\n' +
          '```\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Lists some or all (up to 1,000) objects from the S3 Bucket. Objects are returned in [lexicographical order](https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/search/spl2-search-manual/sort-and-order/lexicographical-order).\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Arguments:\n' +
          '  * `options`\n' +
          '    * `Delimiter` - character used to group keys. For more information, see [Organizing objects using prefixes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-prefixes.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '    * `EncodingType` - encoding type of the [object keys](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-keys.html) in the response. If specified as `url`, object keys in the response use [percent-encoding](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-2.1).\n' +
          '    * `MaxKeys` - maximum number of keys returned in the response. Defaults to `1000`.\n' +
          '    * `Prefix` - limits the response to keys that begin with the specified prefix.\n' +
          '    * `ContinuationToken` - indicates to Amazon S3 that the list is being continued on this bucket with a token. Used to paginate list results.\n' +
          '    * `FetchOwner` - whether the `Owner` field indicating the owner of the object will be present with each key in the response.\n' +
          '    * `StartAfter` - the key after which Amazon S3 will start listing in [lexicographical order](https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/search/spl2-search-manual/sort-and-order/lexicographical-order).\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Return:\n' +
          '  * `data`\n' +
          '    * `IsTruncated` - set to `true` if there are more keys available in the bucket to retrieve.\n' +
          '    * `Contents` - data and metadata about each object returned.\n' +
          '      * `Key` - a name or path that uniquely identifies the object. For more information, see [Naming Amazon S3 objects](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-keys.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '      * `LastModified` - creation date of the object.\n' +
          '      * `ETag` - the entity tag or MD5 hash of the object.\n' +
          '      * `ChecksumAlgorithm`- indicates the algorithm used to create the [checksum](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_Checksum.html) of the object. For more information, see [Checking object integrity in Amazon S3](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/checking-object-integrity.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '      * `Size` - size or data length in bytes of the object.\n' +
          '      * `StorageClass` - the [storage class](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-class-intro.html) associated with the object. Defaults to `STANDARD`.\n' +
          '      * `Owner` - the owner of the object.\n' +
          '        * `DisplayName` - the display name of the owner.\n' +
          '        * `ID` - the ID of the owner.\n' +
          '    * `CommonPrefixes` - common prefixes of keys returned in place of the actual keys. Used to browse keys hierachically. For more information, see [Organizing objects using prefixes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-prefixes.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '      * `Prefix` - the value for a common prefix.\n' +
          '    * `KeyCount` - actual number of keys in the response.\n' +
          '    * `NextContinuationToken` - indicates there are more keys available in the bucket to be listed. To continue the list, this value should be used as the `ContinuationToken` for the next list objects request.\n' +
          '\n' +
          '```javascript\n' +
          'const data1 = await myBucket.listObjects()\n' +
          '\n' +
          'const data2 = await myBucket.listObjects({\n' +
          "  Prefix: 'my-prefix'\n" +
          '})\n' +
          '```',
