        docs: '```coffeescript [specscript]\n' +
          'listObjectVersions(options {\n' +
          '  Delimiter: string,\n' +
          "  EncodingType: 'url',\n" +
          '  KeyMarker: string,\n' +
          '  MaxKeys: number,\n' +
          '  Prefix: string,\n' +
          '  VersionIdMarker: string,\n' +
          '}) -> response Promise<{\n' +
          '  IsTruncated: boolean,\n' +
          '  Versions: Array<{\n' +
          '    IsLatest: boolean,\n' +
          '    Key: string,\n' +
          '    LastModified: Date,\n' +
          '    ETag: string,\n' +
          "    ChecksumAlgorithm: 'CRC32'|'CRC32C'|'SHA1'|'SHA256',\n" +
          "    ChecksumType: 'COMPOSITE'|'FULL_OBJECT',\n" +
          '    Size: number, # bytes\n' +
          "    StorageClass: 'STANDARD'|'REDUCED_REDUNDANCY'|'STANDARD_IA'|'ONEZONE_IA'\n" +
          "                  |'INTELLIGENT_TIERING'|'GLACIER'|'DEEP_ARCHIVE'|'OUTPOSTS'\n" +
          "                  |'GLACIER_IR'|'SNOW'|'EXPRESS_ONEZONE',\n" +
          '    Owner: {\n' +
          '      DisplayName: string,\n' +
          '      ID: string\n' +
          '    },\n' +
          '    VersionId: string,\n' +
          '  }>,\n' +
          '  DeleteMarkers: Array<{\n' +
          '    IsLatest: boolean,\n' +
          '    Key: string,\n' +
          '    LastModified: Date,\n' +
          '    Owner: {\n' +
          '      DisplayName: string,\n' +
          '      ID: string\n' +
          '    },\n' +
          '    VersionId: string,\n' +
          '  }>,\n' +
          '  CommonPrefixes: Array<{ Prefix: string }>,\n' +
          '  NextKeyMarker: string,\n' +
          '  NextVersionIdMarker: string,\n' +
          '}>\n' +
          '```\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Lists some or all (up to 1,000) object versions from the S3 Bucket. Object versions are returned in [lexicographical order](https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/search/spl2-search-manual/sort-and-order/lexicographical-order).\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Arguments:\n' +
          '  * `options`\n' +
          '    * `Delimiter` - character used to group keys. For more information, see [Organizing objects using prefixes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-prefixes.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '    * `EncodingType` - encoding type of the [object keys](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-keys.html) in the response. If specified as `url`, object keys in the response use [percent-encoding](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-2.1).\n' +
          '    * `KeyMarker` - key to start with when listing object versions\n' +
          '    * `MaxKeys` - maximum number of object versions returned in the response. Defaults to `1000`.\n' +
          '    * `Prefix` - limits the response to keys that begin with the specified prefix.\n' +
          '    * `VersionIdMarker` - object version id to start with when listing object versions\n' +
          '\n' +
          'Return:\n' +
          '  * `data`\n' +
          '    * `IsTruncated` - set to `true` if there are more object versions available in the bucket to retrieve.\n' +
          '    * `Versions` - data and metadata about each object version returned.\n' +
          '      * `IsLatest` - whether this object version is the latest version of the object. If `false`, this object version is not the latest version of the object.\n' +
          '      * `Key` - a name or path that, along with the VersionId uniquely identifies the object version.\n' +
          '      * `LastModified` - date and time when the object was last modified.\n' +
          '      * `ETag` - the entity tag or MD5 hash of the object.\n' +
          "      * `ChecksumType` - checksum type (`'COMPOSITE'` or `'FULL_OBJECT'`) that is used to calcuulate the object version's checksum value.\n" +
          '      * `ChecksumAlgorithm`- indicates the algorithm used to create the [checksum](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_Checksum.html) of the object. For more information, see [Checking object integrity in Amazon S3](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/checking-object-integrity.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '      * `Size` - size or data length in bytes of the object.\n' +
          '      * `StorageClass` - the [storage class](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/storage-class-intro.html) associated with the object. Defaults to `STANDARD`.\n' +
          '      * `Owner` - the owner of the object.\n' +
          '        * `DisplayName` - the display name of the owner.\n' +
          '        * `ID` - the ID of the owner.\n' +
          '      * `VersionId` - Version ID of the object version.\n' +
          '    * `DeleteMarkers` - data and metadata about each delete marker returned.\n' +
          '      * `IsLatest` - whether this delete marker is the latest version of the object. If `false`, this delete marker is not the latest version of the object.\n' +
          '      * `Key` - a name or path that, along with the VersionId, uniquely identifies the delete marker.\n' +
          '      * `LastModified` - date and time when the object was last modified.\n' +
          '      * `Owner` - the owner of the object.\n' +
          '        * `DisplayName` - the display name of the owner.\n' +
          '        * `ID` - the ID of the owner.\n' +
          '      * `VersionId` - Version ID of the object version.\n' +
          '    * `CommonPrefixes` - common prefixes of keys returned in place of the actual keys. Used to browse keys hierachically. For more information, see [Organizing objects using prefixes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-prefixes.html) from the _Amazon S3 User Guide_.\n' +
          '      * `Prefix` - the value for a common prefix.\n' +
          '    * `NextKeyMarker` - the key of the object version at which to start the next page of object versions.\n' +
          '    * `NextVersionIdMarker` - the Version ID of the object version at which to start the next page of object versions.\n' +
          '\n' +
          '```javascript\n' +
          'const data1 = await myBucket.listObjectVersions()\n' +
          '\n' +
          "const data2 = await myBucket.listObjectVersions({ Prefix: 'my-prefix })\n" +
          '```',
